# Claude Code / agent worktree artifacts
# `.claude/` stays ignored at every depth (worktrees, settings.local.json, session
# state) EXCEPT the build-loop scaffolding at the repo root, which is committed on
# purpose (queue item 29). Git cannot re-include a file inside an ignored DIRECTORY,
# so the directory's CONTENTS are ignored (`**/.claude/*`) and the four committed
# paths are negated back in. Anything else added under `.claude/` stays ignored.
**/.claude/*
!/.claude/settings.json
!/.claude/commands/
!/.claude/agents/
!/.claude/scripts/
.clone/
new-dashboard/.claude/
new-dashboard/.claire/

# PM2 logs
logs/

# Local-only dev artifacts and session notes
*.local.md

# Local-only identifiers and Entra app metadata (non-secret IDs, but keep out of git)
.local/

# Certificates / private keys — NEVER commit (real keys live outside the repo)
*.pfx
*.cer
*.crt
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
secrets/
**/secrets/

# Container-parity working env (DEV throwaway values; commit the .example only)
deploy/container/.env.container

# RCM section 10/11 staging-walk artifacts. The manifest names live Open Dental
# rows and the two synthetic 835s carry the test patient chart name, so neither
# belongs in git; the scripts that produce them do.
#
# These now default to /data/rcm-s10 (the AzureFile volume) rather than into the
# repo -- /app is read-only in the container. The rule stays so that a local run
# with S10_OUT_DIR pointed back at the old path still cannot commit a manifest.
backend/scripts/out/
